      "problem": "Factor the polynomial expression $p({s}^{2}-11)-12({s}^{2}-11).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the $\\text{GCF}$ of the two terms:\n\n$$\n\\text{GCF}(p({s}^{2}-11),12({s}^{2}-11))={s}^{2}-11\n$$\n\nEach term is already written as a product with the $\\text{GCF}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot ({s}^{2}-11)-12\\cdot ({s}^{2}-11)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the $\\text{GCF}$ outside the parentheses and keep the remaining terms inside:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot ({s}^{2}-11)-12\\cdot ({s}^{2}-11) & = \\\\ (p-12)({s}^{2}-11) & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
